From 4d39bcb0ba23e7a8ae337adc6ee981912ed845af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:42:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: match late CPU expected pair by model

The exact expected pair carries the prior-cycle MIDR revision,
while expected_target_midr records the CPU model used by
capability classification. Generic completeness incorrectly
required the two representations to be byte-identical.

Compare them at their shared model granularity. Keep the exact
pair and later target-register comparison unchanged, along with
every CPU, power, retry, storage, and CPU9 path.
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/late_cpu_profile.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/late_cpu_profile.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/late_cpu_profile.c
index f3b6de4..17f83b8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/late_cpu_profile.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/late_cpu_profile.c
@@ -1722,7 +1722,7 @@ arm64_late_cpu_expected_pair_complete(const struct arm64_late_cpu_plan *plan)
 		if (!expected->capsule_identity[target] ||
 		    expected->mpidr[target] !=
 			    plan->evidence.expected_target_mpidr[target] ||
-		    expected->midr !=
+		    (expected->midr & MIDR_CPU_MODEL_MASK) !=
 			    plan->evidence.expected_target_midr[target])
 			return false;
 
